; The planner test: the one test below nx's public API. Law 3 makes the thread
; count invisible from Nx, so the test calls the C entry points with an explicit
; plan thread count. test_planner.ml redeclares those externals; the type
; checker cannot compare them with the C stubs, so a drift between the two is
; undefined behaviour, not a compile error. Keep them in step with kernels.ml.

(test
 (name test_planner)
 (package nx)
 (libraries nx.cpu nx.array nx.backend nx.dtype nx.device windtrap))
